      "text": "To find the value of \\( t \\) given that the roots of the cubic equation \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\) are \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\), and the roots of \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we start by using Vieta's formulas.\n\nFirst, for the cubic \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), Vieta's formulas tell us:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to express \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\) in terms of \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\). By Vieta's formulas applied to \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we have:\n\\[\na+b = c\n\\]\n\\[\nb+c = a\n\\]\n\\[\nc+a = b\n\\]\n\nAdding these three equations together, we get:\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a) = c + a + b\n\\]\n\\[\n2(a + b + c) = a + b + c\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-3) = -3\n\\]\nThis equation seems incorrect and suggests we need to re-evaluate our approach. Instead, we use a different method to find \\( t \\).\n\nFrom the roots \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\) in terms of \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\), we know:\n\\[\na + (a+b) = c + b\n\\]\n\\[\nb + (b+c) = a + c\n\\]\n\\[\nc + (c+a) = a + b\n\\]\n\nThese equations imply:\n\\[\n2a + a + b = c + b\n\\]\n\\[\nc + c + a = a + c\n\\]\n\\[\n2c + a + b = a + b\n\\]\n\nSimplifying these, we get:\n\\[\n3a = c\n\\]\n\\[\n2c = a\n\\]\nThis is not generally true without specific values. Instead, we need to use a different method to relate \\( t \\) to the original roots. We know that:\n\\[\n(r - abc) = t \\quad \\text{and} \\quad s = -(abc)\n\\]\nGiven \\( abc = 11 \\), we have:\n\\[\ns = -11\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we need \\( t \\) in terms of the sum of the roots of the second polynomial:\n\\[\na + b + (a + b) = 2(a + b)\n\\]\nSince \\( a + b = c \\), we have:\n\\[\nt = (a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a)\n\\]\n\\[\nt = 2(a + b) + 2(a + b) = 6(a + b)\n\\]\n\nGiven \\( a + b = c \\), we substitute \\( c = b \\) and solve:\n\\[\nt = 6(a + b) = 6(c)\n\\]\n\nSince \\( c = b \\) and \\( b = a \\), we realize the sum of the roots of the second polynomial is:\n\\[\n(a + b) + (b + c) + (c + a) = (a + b) + (b + b) + (b + a) = 3(a + b)\n\\]\nGiven \\( a + b = c \\) and \\( c = b \\), we solve directly:\n\\[\nt = 3(a + b) = 3((a + b) - a + (a + b) - b) = 3(a + b - a) = 3b\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( t \\) is:\n\\[\nt = 3(a + b)\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-11}\n\\]",
